\f4\fs26 The Johnny was none too happy when he was dragged into Police H.Q. by a couple of uniformed rock-apes. He had never had occasion to speak to a low life-walloper for any reason, nor had he harboured any no desire to do so. He had made the mistake of refusing their kind invitation outright and slammed his door in their unsmiling faces. A mistake that was something, shortly thereafter, as they dragged him into the elevator and down to street level, he came to regret. To his credit he concluded antagonising the cops any further would be counter-productive to future breathing and metabolic functions and he offered up no further resistance. The silent gorillas physically carried him to a tiny office where Sarah was smugly seated behind an embarrassingly small desk.\
\'93Sarah? This is your new contract? Public Service? I can\'92t believe you were behind this. They assaulted me! On your instructions, no less.\'94 Johnny was not happy, but he was never happy about anything, ever. \'93Whatever you want, I am not interested.\'94\
\'93Thank you for taking up my invitation, Johnny. I really need your help again.\'94 Sarah placed an evidence bag on the desk.\
\'93Invitation? They dragged me here.\'94 He picked up the plastic bag and eyes widened with fright when he saw the Gyges disc inside. \'93No, No. I am not going down that road again. Not for you, not for anyone.\'94\
\'93C\'92mon Johnny. You can examine the disc with the blessing of the PTD police department. It is still top secret, but there will be no legal ramifications and no damage to your reputation.\'94\
\'93I am worried about damage to my body,\'94 He gingerly ran his fingers along the length of the red-raw scar atop his crown. \'93Not my reputation.\'94\
\'93It gives you character, Johnny. Besides, I told you to behave yourself and you dismissed my advice outright.\'94 Sarah counselled. \'93Perhaps you might want to listen in future.\'94\
\'93I see they have rewarded you for shooting that low-life cleaner. What a lovely office.\'94 His sarcasm was exaggerated and unmistakable. \
\'93No, this is your new office. For a couple of days, anyway.\'94 Sarah tried desperately not to laugh, but the look of horror on Johnny\'92s face was just priceless and she had to let go with a giggle.\
\'93Not on your life, Sarah. I am not staying here. Goodbye.\'94 He turned and walked out the door and was immediately escorted back by the two large uniforms.\
\'93Johnny, you will be expected to examine this disc and compare it with the first one we located. Okay? We want to know what it is, what it does and where it was manufactured. This part is important, so listen carefully. The information we have is that the discs are, indeed, powered by gravity waves and they must never come into close contact with one another or spun in the centre axis or you run the risk of creating a gravity well. They is the only limitations on your examinations. Apart from that you have carte-blanche to do whatever you deem fit.\'94\
\'93In that case, let me at it.\'94 Johnny was still in sarcasm mode. \'93A gravity well, what could possibly go wrong?\'94\
\'93I want you because you have a some experience with these discs. If you don\'92t want to help I will get someone else. Do you know anyone else you would trust to do the work?\'94 Sarah knew appealing to his ego would bring him around. \'93There has to be someone else. Someone smarter than you, perhaps?\'94\
\'93Very funny. As far as I can tell, there isn\'92t anyone smarter that me.\'94 Johnny\'92s pride took hold. \'93Nobody I know would have the talent.\'94\
\'93There must be someone else, but...\'94 Sarah knew she had him. \'93You are the only one I can trust. Anyone else might destroy us.\'94\
\'93I will need a fully fitted out lab and at least 3 assistants.\'94\
\'93There\'92s two labs in the forensic facility, one for each disc, with six assistants awaiting your instructions. You will collect the other disc and bring it in.\'94 \
\'93I will only do it if I get paid more than you.\'94 He didn\'92t care how much, just as long as it was more than Sarah.\
\'93It\'92s a deal.\'94 Sarah did not really mind who was paid more, she was really cleaning up and had no problem with Johnny getting amongst the lucre. \'93Go fetch the disc now. There is a possibility the company agents may try to steal it back, so be careful. The two constables outside will escort you there and back. They have been instructed to protect you with their lives. You are now officially on contract to this department, and until all your tests are complete you are a contemptible public servant, just like me.\'94 She again allowed herself to giggle at Johnny as embarrassment and anguish comically distorted his chubby pale face.\
\'93This will not look good on a resume.\'94 He knew that wasn\'92t true. If it was okay for corporations to squeeze the state dry, it was certainly okay for him. The private sector had a long and questionable history of sucking at the public teat and who was he to criticise?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0

