\f3 \cf0 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f4\fs26 Director Hardman sat at the head of a long conference table, chairing the first meeting of his highly secretive team tasked with retrieving viral agents from the Hardy Bio-Weapons facility. Damien had given the briefing a couple of days before and let his minions digest the enormity of the assignment. He now expected some brilliant ideas as to how they could dig through 40 metres of rock and 10 metres of concrete without raising any suspicion and recovering the bio-agents without starting a second viral cleansing. \
Agent Jones sat quietly, trying not to look guilty while, at the same time, not too relaxed either, but with four shattered ribs he was in no danger of looking relaxed. The feeling of being compromised by an external agency sickened him. He had always been a company man and spying for the police was not a comfortable fit. He wanted desperately to cleanse his soul and tell the Director about his encounter with the PTD Police, but that would be suicide. Not only would he have to confess to losing another disc, he would have to admit to being beaten up by a slender beauty queen. His ego would not let him look there. \
\'93Director, are you able to tell us why we are digging up something so dangerous?\'94 Agent Kimberley asked innocently.\
\'93I have not been able to tell you until now, until all your security checks and transfer orders had been completed. Now I can unequivocally say, ladies and gentlemen, you are the elite of the agency and have been selected for this task due to your commitment to freedom and democracy.\'94 
\f5\i Also because you are all so eminently disposable, he thought.
\f4\i0  \'93The Primary Trade Dominion faces the greatest peril since its formation 50 years ago. There is a cancer, creeping silently through our souls, eating away at our very way of life. This cancer is the Elvi.\'94 \
\'93Surely not, Director. They are just entertainers, aren\'92t they?\'94 Agent Kimberly again showed his naivety. Director Hardman decided this guy would be the first to go.\
\'93That is precisely what they want us all to think. That they are merely a lovable bunch of singers, dancers and bartenders, whose sole purpose for being is to entertain us, but they are nothing of the sort. They organise and conspire against the PTD. Their concerts are filled with subversive political commentary aimed at undermining the natural order and to ultimately change the structure of our society, placing themselves at the top. The lyrics to many songs are direct threats to vital industries that thrive under our deregulated system. Coal producers are livid and they are threatening mass sackings if something is not done. It\'92s the same with the power companies.\'94\
\'93Can\'92t we just kill them? It sounds like doctrinal divergence to me.\'94 Agent Jones wanted to be the first to offer up that option. He knew it was a ridiculous suggestion, but he wanted to sound hard core in front of his juniors.\
\'93No, we can\'92t kill them. Not directly. There are too many and it would be too costly. Not only that, for every Elvis there are five Dawks who would no doubt riot.\'94 \
\'93What is the plan, boss?\'94 Agent Jones knew when to suck up.\
\'93The Bio-weapons labs that we are breaking into were working on viral agents targeting one specific genome, one specific target. We are going to recover that research and if we are lucky, safely recover some samples. It is hoped that our scientists will be able to complete the research. A virus that targets one Elvis, targets all the Elvi.\'94\
\'93We are going to kill them after all.\'94 Agent Jones was all smiles. He would be involved in an actual genocide! Wow! That will look good on a resume, he automatically thought, before being brought back to earth by the reality he was now a Barbie doll\'92s bitch and promotion prospects were grim. He had seen her shoot the cleaner on Random Camera, but he could have sworn, two hours before, she would have given her life to protect him. There was no way he was crossing a crazy, fickle bitch like her.\
\'93I will now introduce you to Professor James Ararie, PhD, Fellow of the International College of Bio-engineers, L.5.\'94 The Director sat down and left the pointy head to illuminate his collection of dullards on the finer points of micro-biology. The only information they really needed to know was how to identify the specimens and transport them safely. Unfortunately they were all about to sit through a four hour lecture comprised of scientific gobbledygook and intellectual self indulgence.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_Ps::0>
\f2 * * *\
\pard\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\pardeftab720\fi360\sl264\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f4\fs26 With trust in their police colleagues completely evaporated, Hayley and Sarah, decided to rendezvous with Agent Jones in the quarter, using Elvi as surveillance and security. The Minister for Internal Security had given them a team of 50 Elvis and Elvine operatives to secure the area, expelling any non-Elvis in a 200 metre radius. Neither company agent nor cop could get close, even if Agent Jones was tailed. Upon crossing the security perimeter he was blindfolded and taken before the Blessed Mother and Holy Aunt Hayley.\
His vision returned with a violent jerk of the blindfold. Agent Jones was seated on single chair in the centre of an abandoned auditorium with at least 10 Elvi standing along each wall, vacantly staring ahead. Hayley threw the piece of dark cloth on the floor and stood silent behind him while Sarah stood directly in front, 2 metres distant.\
\'93You said you had something for us?\'94 Sarah stepped forward.\
\'93Yes, but I don\'92t think it should be said with your entourage within earshot.\'94 He leaned back in his chair and away from the advancing Blessed Mother.\
\'93Could all Elvi please wait outside?\'94 Sarah asked in her best Blessed Mother voice. She had not quite perfected it yet, but she was going for a soft, serene and confident monotone. Without a word the room cleared in a choreographed military dance.\
\'93I have found out why they are digging up the bio-weapons labs. They are planning to release a virus and kill off the Elvi.\'94 He delivered with a smirk and a sickening tone of approval.\
\'93Won\'92t they kill everyone else?\'94 Sarah did not allow her alarm to ripple the calm surface. \
\'93They plan to target the Elvi genome specifically. Our scientists are in their labs just waiting for the samples and the research data, practicing their gene transfer procedures. They have already cooked up some new and deadly pathogens and plan to eventually kidnap a group of Elvi, to conduct tests, but at the moment the Bio-Engineers are confident they have more than enough data to make significant headway.\'94\
\'93How long will it take to drill down?\'94 Hayley asked.\
\'93We haven\'92t even started yet. The security issues alone will take a month. Transferring that shit to another facility will be a nightmare. They haven\'92t even manufactured the canisters yet. I\'92ve got the plans for them in my implant if you want to download them.\'94\
\'93I have been trying to get maps and blueprints for all the buildings in that area and can\'92t get hold of anything. I keep getting told the buildings are so old the plans have not been digitised, but that\'92s bureaucrat-speak for classified.\'94 Hayley did not like being thwarted by her own employer.\
\'93I have those plans too.\'94\
\'93Good work, Agent Jones.\'94 Sarah was genuine, but Hayley remained silent. \'93We will see you next week. Make sure you contact us if they start drilling.\'94\
\'93Yes, Mrs Shakti.\'94 Agent Jones smiled and looked directly at her, unblinking.\
\'93Yes, I am to be allocated to the son of Eloise Shakti.\'94 Sarah fired back, pleased his sudden discomfort showed her salvo had hit her target. No-one wanted to cross Eloise Shakti. \'93Yes, you have yet another woman to fear.\'94 \
\'93I will report anything of interest and download all the documents I can.\'94 His courage melted away as his spine returned to its natural gelatinous state.\
\'93They are on a deadline and will be moving fast. We will have to react just as quickly and somehow get ahead of them.\'94 Sarah stood perfectly still, staring into Agent Jones\'92 eyes, hoping he comprehended the urgency of this unfolding situation.\
\'93I understand.\'94 Agent Jones stood up and walked to the door where he was met with his Elvi escort party.\
They waited until they were certain their voices could not be heard. The enormity of what they had been told was hitting hard. Genocide.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

