\f4\fs26 \'93What is your proposal Holy Aunt Hayley?\'94 He had been hoping for a mundane day of kicking back in his office and writing a song or two, but the High Elvis once again found himself mid-crisis. This one was a real beaut, but he was growing as a leader and took it in his stride.\
\'93We have a man on the inside who will slow their progress as best he can and if necessary we can opt for sabotage, but the laboratories and their contents will still be there. Someone else is bound to try. We must be the first into that research complex and we must destroy the samples where they are stored, nothing can be permitted to get out.\'94 Holy Aunt Hayley had no idea how to accomplish this and hoped someone else might have some ideas. Her discussions with Blessed Mother Sarah had not been particularly fruitful. \'93That is my proposal High Elvis. We have to stop this or die trying.\'94\
\'93You will have at your disposal all the resources of the entire Elvi nation. What we lack in technology, we make up for in man power. You must succeed or the Elvi will perish, Holy Aunt.\'94\
\'93Once we have examined the plans for pipes, conduits and tunnels we might be able to work out a way of getting there first. This should be on a need to know basis only. Our success depends entirely on strict security. I hold no fears the Elvi will betray us, but we need them to carry on as if nothing is happening.\'94\
\'93The Elvi will never betray your trust, but I agree, knowledge of the conspiracy would place them in a difficult position. Only those who need to know.\'94 
\f5\i Paternalism now. Is there no line I will not cross? 
\f4\i0 He was fast learning that leadership meant compromising everything, fondly held ideals included. \'93I insist you enlist The Great Teacher to assist in your quest. I fear you think him a buffoon, but he observes from a most obscure angle and he is schooled in the way of the street. He will see what you are unable to see and he can obtain what is out of your reach. I do not think the Blessed Mother will be able to give you all of her attention in the coming months as the arrival of the one-after-the-one approaches. Praise be to the Dawkins.\'94\
\'93He is hardly a replacement for Sarah, High Elvis, but he could be of some assistance.\'94 She didn\'92t think so, but like everyone, else she had been told never to insult an Elvis, particularly the High Elvis. She thought Cracker was a smart-Alec unable to take any situation seriously and apart from his recent resurrection, he had not done anything to impress her. Although she she did quietly admit, resurrection was a pretty good trick.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_Ps::0>
\f2 * * *
\f1 \
\pard\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\pardeftab720\fi360\sl264\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f4\fs26 \'93We have to get into this bunker, through 10 metres of concrete. We need covert access to the site. Any ideas?\'94 Hayley was confident Cracker would be of as much assistance as a gorilla, but for the sake of keeping the High Elvis happy she decided to go through the motions. Cracker reached his right hand over the top of his head and scratched the left ear and hunch over the emitter and then dragged his knuckles across the floor to the far side of the holographic presentation. His little primate brain ticked over as his scratched at his chest and adjusted his groin.\
\'93Yeah, I see your problem, but I think I might have a solution. Do you recognise that building?\'94 Cracker pointed to an old multi storey stone structure. \
\'93No, what of it?\'94 Hayley had no idea where he was going with this. The building was at least 100 metres from the bio-weapons bunker.\
\'93You should recognise it, Detective Lanning. The ground floor and basement was the site for the Stick It Inn nightclub.\'94\
\'93So?\'94\
\'93Don\'92t you see? That is the site of the terrorist bombing.\'94\
\'93I know that.\'94\
\'93They are finishing up the demolition of the building right now and have cleared right down to 3rd sub basement level.\'94 He then waved his hand over the hologram emitter and raised a 3-D map of the city\'92s underground. \'93Look, the sub-basement levels are about the same depth as the bunker. There are a few pipes and conduits in the way, but we could dig across, on top of the sandstone layer, through clay rather than concrete.\'94\
As a matter of policy she wanted to reject the idea of her inferior, but could not immediately poke a hole in the proposal. She and Sarah had been staring at the maps and scratching her their heads for days trying to come up with a plan. Perhaps it was a manifestation of a devious, level 2 type of intelligence, she thought, nothing for her to be concerned about. \'93It\'92s a long way. Do you think we can dig through 100 metres of clay quicker than they can drill through rocks and concrete?\'94 \
\'93I don\'92t know, but I can find out easily. I know a few guys in demolition. You know, the types of people you would never to talk to.\'94 Cracker had been getting a superior vibe from Hayley and wanted her to know it had not gone unnoticed.\
\'93Can you get us on site?\'94 She let his jibe slip through to the wicket-keeper.\
\'93I think I can, but we are going to be there for quite a few days, so we are going to need a pretty good cover story. I mean we can bribe the contractors quite easily, but digging a tunnel of that nature will raise some suspicion. I will speak with the High Elvis.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_Ps::0>
